  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25890212",
      "title": "Working with Props & TypeScript",
      "sourceHash": "404cca60d218e25864f5379bb1943cc5c1222852840ce2ddbdf951beb2fd27b0",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 5.35,
          "en": "So let's delete those hard-coded Todos here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.35,
          "end": 7.78,
          "en": "And now let's say we get some props here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 7.78,
          "end": 12.38,
          "en": "And now my goal is that the props should have items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 14.01,
          "end": 17.01,
          "en": "or Todos prop, where I can then map",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 17.01,
          "end": 21.58,
          "en": "through all those items to then output the list items.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 21.58,
          "end": 23.15,
          "en": "And you can already see here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 23.15,
          "end": 26.74,
          "en": "that now I'm getting those red squiggly lines here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 26.74,
          "end": 30.48,
          "en": "And if we hover over that, we see that prompts is declared",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 30.48,
          "end": 32.73,
          "en": "but it's value is never read.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 32.73,
          "end": 35.7,
          "en": "So we're getting a warning that we're not using props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 35.7,
          "end": 38.3,
          "en": "and that's a little extra help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 38.3,
          "end": 40.37,
          "en": "we get into TypeScript project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 40.37,
          "end": 42.15,
          "en": "which we don't necessarily get",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 42.15,
          "end": 44.73,
          "en": "in a vanilla JavaScript project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 44.73,
          "end": 48.38,
          "en": "We are warned if we have some unnecessary code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 48.38,
          "end": 50.3,
          "en": "code that we're not using.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.3,
          "end": 52.94,
          "en": "And we also get this warning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 52.94,
          "end": 57.383,
          "en": "that the parameter props is implicitly of` type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 58.35,
          "end": 61.75,
          "en": "And that means that we did not assign a type here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.75,
          "end": 65,
          "en": "We're not making it clear which kind of type disease",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 65,
          "end": 67.11,
          "en": "and therefore we're basically not getting",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 67.11,
          "end": 69.46000000000001,
          "en": "any TypeScript support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 69.46000000000001,
          "end": 71.95,
          "en": "And that's why you can configure TypeScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.95,
          "end": 76.47,
          "en": "such that it warns you if you are implicitly using any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 76.47,
          "end": 80.77,
          "en": "If I now explicitly set this to type any, it would be okay.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 80.77,
          "end": 83.94,
          "en": "I'm now explicitly saying I don't have any more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 83.94,
          "end": 87.08,
          "en": "specific information about this props argument;",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 87.08,
          "end": 88.49,
          "en": "it is of type any.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 88.49,
          "end": 91.7,
          "en": "It could be anything and that's then fine.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.7,
          "end": 94.21000000000001,
          "en": "But if you don't set this type explicitly,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 94.21000000000001,
          "end": 96.4,
          "en": "you are implicitly assuming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 96.4,
          "end": 98.78999999999999,
          "en": "that you don't know anything about that type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 98.78999999999999,
          "end": 101.22999999999999,
          "en": "and that's why TypeScript is warning us here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.22999999999999,
          "end": 104.25,
          "en": "We shouldn't make this implicit assumption.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.25,
          "end": 106.47,
          "en": "By the way you can configure the strictness",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 106.47,
          "end": 109.92,
          "en": "of TypeScript here in the tsconfig.json file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 109.92,
          "end": 112.22,
          "en": "But I'll come back to that a little bit later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 113.13,
          "end": 115.03,
          "en": "For the moment what we need to do here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.03,
          "end": 116.75,
          "en": "is we need to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 116.75,
          "end": 119.47,
          "en": "which kind of props we're getting here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 119.47,
          "end": 123.25,
          "en": "what the type of props in this function should be.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 123.25,
          "end": 126.5,
          "en": "And of course, we can do this with a type assignment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 126.5,
          "end": 131.5,
          "en": "And now we could actually say that props is an object type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 132.08,
          "end": 135.01,
          "en": "So we add those curly braces.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 135.01,
          "end": 137.14,
          "en": "And again, that's not a value here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 137.14,
          "end": 139.32,
          "en": "that's a type definition.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 139.32,
          "end": 140.94,
          "en": "It's an object type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 140.94,
          "end": 145.68,
          "en": "and we know that props in React will always be an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 145.68,
          "end": 150.68,
          "en": "with all the attributes we added on our own element here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 150.77,
          "end": 155.09,
          "en": "in App.tsx as key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 155.09,
          "end": 155.94,
          "en": "So here we could say",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.94,
          "end": 160.49,
          "en": "that we expect to get some Todos or some items",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.49,
          "end": 163.3,
          "en": "and then in turn could be an array of strings,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 163.3,
          "end": 165.3,
          "en": "let's say like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.3,
          "end": 168.23,
          "en": "That's how we could say that props is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.23,
          "end": 169.75,
          "en": "with the items key,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 169.75,
          "end": 173.323,
          "en": "which then itself holds an array of strings as a value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 175.06,
          "end": 179.12,
          "en": "But that would actually not be 100% correct.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.12,
          "end": 183.05,
          "en": "Props does not just have the key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.05,
          "end": 187.96,
          "en": "we added on our component when we use it in JSX.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.96,
          "end": 190.33,
          "en": "Instead, props is an object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.33,
          "end": 193.26,
          "en": "which does have those key value pairs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 193.26,
          "end": 198.19,
          "en": "But remember that they're also always as a special prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.19,
          "end": 200.55,
          "en": "the children prop",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.55,
          "end": 203.94,
          "en": "and we don't even know the type of that yet.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 203.94,
          "end": 206.18,
          "en": "Now we could find out which type that should be",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.18,
          "end": 207.82999999999998,
          "en": "and then added like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 207.82999999999998,
          "end": 210.57,
          "en": "but it would quickly become cumbersome",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 210.57,
          "end": 213.34,
          "en": "if for every component that we're defining",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 213.34,
          "end": 215.01,
          "en": "that is using props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 215.01,
          "end": 219.8,
          "en": "we have to always add those built-in props to that object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.8,
          "end": 222.6,
          "en": "and then also our custom props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 222.6,
          "end": 224.59,
          "en": "And because that's cumbersome,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 224.59,
          "end": 228.69,
          "en": "and because we have that base prop object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 228.69,
          "end": 230.53,
          "en": "which we get an every component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 230.53,
          "end": 233.43,
          "en": "which for example includes this children prop,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 235.57,
          "en": "React gives us a different way here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 235.57,
          "end": 239.54,
          "en": "or React and TypeScript gives us a different way here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 239.54,
          "end": 243.593,
          "en": "We can use such a generic type, which you might remember.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 244.72,
          "end": 248.3,
          "en": "We can use such a generic type or to be precise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.3,
          "end": 251.91,
          "en": "a functional component out of the box",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.91,
          "end": 256.91,
          "en": "can be turned, can be converted into a generic function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 258.24,
          "end": 260.86,
          "en": "Which then simply means that in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 260.86,
          "end": 263.32,
          "en": "our functional component will be configured",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 263.32,
          "end": 265.06,
          "en": "such that we make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 265.06,
          "end": 267.8,
          "en": "that it will be our React component function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 267.8,
          "end": 272.04,
          "en": "and that it will have all those base props like children.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 272.04,
          "end": 275.64,
          "en": "And we can then define explicitly our own props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 275.64,
          "end": 278.5,
          "en": "like the items prop, for example, here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 278.5,
          "end": 282.36,
          "en": "that should be combined into the props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 282.36,
          "end": 285.07,
          "en": "And if that's not 100% clear yet,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 285.07,
          "end": 286.96,
          "en": "I'll show you how it works.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 286.96,
          "end": 290.43,
          "en": "We can actually write this a little bit differently",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 290.43,
          "end": 293.31,
          "en": "and use this arrow function syntax",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 293.31,
          "end": 296.65,
          "en": "which we used throughout this course all the time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 296.65,
          "end": 298.64,
          "en": "So that our Todos constant here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 298.64,
          "end": 301.59,
          "en": "holds this React component function.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 301.59,
          "end": 306.15,
          "en": "And now we can assign a type here to this Todos constant.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 306.15,
          "end": 309.01,
          "en": "And the type here should actually be React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 309.01,
          "end": 311.13,
          "en": "for which we need to import React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 311.13,
          "end": 315.793,
          "en": "from React like this, dot FC.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 317.92,
          "end": 321.7,
          "en": "Now that's a type defined in this React package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 321.7,
          "end": 325.53,
          "en": "or to be precise by this typesreact package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 325.53,
          "end": 328.11,
          "en": "but we can just import React from React",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 328.11,
          "end": 330.57,
          "en": "and the rest will be done behind the scenes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 330.57,
          "end": 333.35,
          "en": "So this is a type definition here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 333.35,
          "end": 336.02,
          "en": "Now, if I hold Cmd and click on this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 336.02,
          "end": 340.03,
          "en": "or Ctrl and click on this, I see the type definition here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 340.03,
          "end": 342.06,
          "en": "And I see that it's a function component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 342.06,
          "end": 344.51,
          "en": "which is yet another type definition built",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 344.51,
          "end": 346.113,
          "en": "into this React package.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 347.6,
          "end": 351.33,
          "en": "Now what React.FC in the end does as a type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 351.33,
          "end": 355.61,
          "en": "is it makes it clear that this here is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 355.61,
          "end": 358.3,
          "en": "that acts as a functional component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 358.3,
          "end": 362.65,
          "en": "That's what FC stands for functional component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 362.65,
          "end": 365.79,
          "en": "And you see that now the red squiggly lines for props",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 365.79,
          "end": 367.34,
          "en": "are gone.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 367.34,
          "end": 371.05,
          "en": "And if I now try to use props here in my JSX code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 371.05,
          "end": 375.21,
          "en": "and I add a dot, I see that I now get this auto-completion",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 375.21,
          "end": 377.99,
          "en": "for the children props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 377.99,
          "end": 381.33,
          "en": "So now, simply by adding this type annotation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 381.33,
          "end": 384.55,
          "en": "in TypeScript and my IDE therefore,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 384.55,
          "end": 386.88,
          "en": "which is very smart about that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 386.88,
          "end": 389.7,
          "en": "understands that this is a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 389.7,
          "end": 392.23,
          "en": "that receives a props object",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 392.23,
          "end": 394.42,
          "en": "as an argument, as a first argument,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 394.42,
          "end": 399.05,
          "en": "which will be an object that always has a children property,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 399.05,
          "end": 401.58,
          "en": "a children field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 401.58,
          "end": 404.23,
          "en": "And it understands does it knows this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 404.23,
          "end": 406.283,
          "en": "because of this type assignment here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 407.18,
          "end": 409.96,
          "en": "Now I mentioned that generic types would be important",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 409.96,
          "end": 413.29,
          "en": "because this is actually a generic type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 413.29,
          "end": 416.37,
          "en": "and we can now merge our own type definition",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 416.37,
          "end": 417.76,
          "en": "for it as props object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 417.76,
